<title>USA: OUTLOOK - Poor margins cut back US MTBE production.</title>
<headline>OUTLOOK - Poor margins cut back US MTBE production.</headline>
<byline>Laney Salisbury</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Gulf MTBE producers are cutting back this month because the high cost of feedstocks combined with low prices make operating a losing proposition, analysts said Friday.</p>
<p>Analysts estimate that for January U.S. production will be down by 45,000 to 60,000 barrels per day, or 23 percent of total U.S. demand of 260,000 bpd.</p>
